the power of wolves and wolf dogs to  help people heal it's a hybrid animal  the wolf dog by the way got the genes of  both animals and in southern california  there's a unique wild animal sanctuary  giving at-risk teens a chance to work  with rescued wolves and wolf dogs the  goal is to help young people learn  valuable life lessons about forgiveness  acceptance and i would say above all  trust in this case jonathan biglyhotty  saw the impact of this wolf therapy  firsthand  at an animal sanctuary in the mountains  north of los angeles the haunting howl  of a wolf  comes to life  she she's not shy i've never been looked  by a wolf before  i think i've actually enjoyed falling  teo alfero runs wolf connection and  spends his days rescuing and  rehabilitating wolf dogs these two came  from came to us as pubs and we've been  loving them since so neither one of  these no not the bad side of humans  some other wolves that we have here are  like i said shy and skittish but none of  them are vicious this is gemma alfaro  who studies the animal's behavior says  science supports what indigenous tribes  have long recognized that humans and  wolves have been working together for  tens of thousands of years  so the wolf helped us activate a primal  side of us  that is more connected more grounded  more clear-minded we consider the wolf  the healer of the human heart  alfaro nurtured the wolves he then  created the first wolf therapy model a  holistic approach that helps both the  abused wolves and teens and he says it's  been 100 percent safe for program  participants people some of your  audience would go what if a kid gets  mauled by a wolf right we put thousands  of hours on each wall before they become  part of the program and in 13 years we  have a zero incident history in order to  be okay with who i am i need to know who  i am amanda bier a licensed psychologist  is the program's director when we talk  about release it's really about  acceptance in this exercise teens choose  a rock i got mine that embodies their  inner turmoil then lug that burden up  the mountain  it's my stress  like the wolves many here carry  emotional scars and feel hurt angry and  alone so the wolves that come here have  an array of trauma and we see the same  thing in the youth that come here from  severe physical abuse neglect sexual  abuse and then also young people who  have never been able to be seen  because the humans in their life want  them to be something other than who they  are she shares stories of the resilience  of wolves it's just natural  for wolves to accept the past  to make room for new things then the  teens symbolically release their pain  when edward amaya enrolled in wolfe  connection's eight-week program he  carried the weight of witnessing his  uncle's murder as a kid i lost a lot of  people  i watched family members pass away i had  my only uncle that took care of me in my  arms pass away i held on to those deaths  very  close i think that's probably why i  didn't  socialize because i didn't want that to  happen again reluctant at first he  joined the pack around a medicine wheel  a sacred space where it's believed the  body and spirit come together for  healing i just started crying and  everything just came out it was a big  turn for me being able to do that  just being in the presence of wolves has  been life-changing for many of these  teens julia gomez says she felt  neglected as a child and today battles  anxiety and depression  [Music]  but the poise and power of this wolf  annie inspired her to push on  even though she was  missing one of her limbs  she was still a warrior  and which really connected to me she  gave me the courage to to keep  persevering  [Music]  amaya and gomez are now working at wolf  connection knowing firsthand how the  program helped them to grow  regret  and what was that moment like and you  released  all of that it  felt like i just let like a hundred  pounds off my shoulders it felt like a  new power like it felt like a superpower  almost we call it hiking for the wolves  is migrating hiking with  wolves hearing them howl  leads to breakthroughs every day you can  see it in their face they're almost like  oh in that moment you saw  humans change in that moment i saw  miracles happening right in front of my  eyes for cbs mornings i'm jonathan  vigliotti in palmdale california  what an unexpectedly powerful and moving  really i love the idea of accepting the  past to make room for the future yeah i  never thought of it that way it's so  true  and we all know that the strength of a  wolf is its pack and they're stronger  because of that and i think that  representation for individuals going  through something is that you do need  people and you can lean on other people  to help make you stronger even when you  feel weak i like where he said they're  shy and skittish but never vicious  because i think when you look at them  you think are they going to turn but he  said they've never had an incident 13  years never had a problem and when you  say that i've seen miracles happen in  person very seldom did we get to see  that you're right very nice job jonathan  bigliotti
 

